From 040735ddb1b61f501494e5bbc120ab7ad5a50db2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sixvolts <rigel@sixvolts.org>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:41:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: loads-first dense K-quant / Q8_0 matvecs and Q4_K GLU
 on GCN (crossport R10)

Rows are clamped (min(row, ne1-1)) with a masked store instead of 'if (row >= ne1) continue', and
both rows' planes are loaded before the first dot, so the memory system sees every row's stream at
once (reinstinct 54eaa04): mul_mat_vec_q4k/q5k/q6k_repacked, the generic mul_mat_vec_q8_0_repacked
and the dense Q4_K gate+up GLU. The K-quant kernels get __launch_bounds__(256). The dense Q4_K
matvec and GLU add a scheduling barrier after the hoisted loads (crossport P1b: without it the
compiler re-splits each trip into load / wait / dot); it stays Q4_K-only and GGML_CUDA_NO_Q4K_FENCE=1
drops it. No spills in any touched kernel (Q4_K 38/47 VGPRs, Q5_K/Q6_K 64, GLU 56/61).

Qwen3.5-4B on one MI50, per call at decode: Q6_K 63.5 -> 53.8 us, Q5_K 32.4 -> 25.8, Q4_K GLU
51.9 -> 41.5 (50.9 without the fence); tg64 UD-Q4_K_XL 116.0 -> 131.5, Q5_K_M 100.8 -> 119.7;
pp512 unchanged. test-repack-bench --check OK on the dense K-quant, Q8_0 and nibble shapes.
The reordered code lets the compiler contract differently, so logits are rounding-close, not
bit-identical: KLD vs the previous build 0.0029 at ub1 (same-top-p 97.8%; the 4B's reorder floor),
PPL 9.501 vs 9.462 / 9.510 vs 9.527 on 2 chunks.

